    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_224c9cca9189c8bfb61785987f13ba9861d1cb97e7f415a7521f1c3803dc9818",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source maps different departures from the U(1)^c scalar channel to different bottlenecks. Eta multiplication restores harmonic-analytic access for Virasoro partition functions but produces all-spin fake scalars with signed character coefficients; applying the zero-annihilating functional then weakens dimension decay enough to compete with Cardy growth. A guessed scalar-only Virasoro rule avoids the all-spin representation only in a numerically supported c<7 regime, whereas an exact fixed-spin projection restores spin information at the price of an additional sporadic Maass cusp-form term.",
