    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_b68f67fdba7436de5c2957a0715dc975e7e502bef05bf71fdab338b40df9d366",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source builds a staged representation pipeline: Roelcke-Selberg decomposition separates Eisenstein and Maass data, scalar x-averaging removes the Maass sector, Eisenstein subtraction makes the reduced U(1)^c partition function square-integrable and packages scalar dimensions in a constrained Epstein transform, and a contour shift converts the transform's gap-constrained poles into zero-indexed powers. After differentiation removes the remaining constant, the Poisson-Mellin functional sends t^s to zeta(s)M_phi(s), so all powers indexed by nontrivial zeta zeros share one exact annihilator.",
